course: dictionary
lesson: 12891
title: Envisage: picturing and planning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Envisage is a formal word. It means to imagine or picture something that might happen in the future. «She envisaged a day when every child had a library card.» She is not looking at a real library. She is picturing one in her mind.
explain: Envisage can also mean to expect or plan something. «We envisage finishing the project by summer» means we plan to finish by summer. You will often find it in news and official writing, such as «The council envisages a new park by the river.»
explain: In a story, you might be asked to envisage the scene: picture where it is, what it looks like and what might happen next. Read the words around envisage to check which meaning fits, then swap your meaning into the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Envisage is a verb: envisage, envisages, envisaged, envisaging.
fact: «Envisage» means to imagine or picture something that might happen in the future.
fact: «Envisage» can also mean to expect or plan something.
fact: It is a formal word, so you will meet it in exams, news and official writing.
fact: Americans often say «envision» instead of «envisage».
exercise: «I envisage a city of gardens on the hill.» What does envisage mean here? | Measure carefully | *Picture or imagine | Forget completely | Dig up
exercise: «The council envisages a new park by the river.» What does envisage mean here? | Feels cold | *Plans or expects | Sells the land | Wrecks the old park
exercise: Which word is the American way of saying envisage? | Dance | Enclose | Envelope | *Envision
test: «We envisage finishing the project by summer.» Which word means about the same as envisage here? | Forget | Sing | *Expect | Stop
test: Mia's teacher asks her to envisage the scene before she writes. What should she do? | Count the words on the page | Copy a page from a book | Close her eyes and go to sleep | *Picture where it is and what might happen
exam: «It is envisaged that the bridge will open next year.» What does envisaged mean? | Painted red | Broken | Forgotten | *Planned or expected
